---
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";

const project = {
    name: "Smart Napf",
    description: "A smart home mobile application for controlling pet food bowls. (Design only)"
}
---

<ProjectLayout description={project.description} title={project.name}>
    <Section slot="show-section">
        <img class="mx-auto" src="/img/cubes/smartnapf.webp" />
    </Section>

    <Section slot="tell-section">
        <div class="p-10">
            <p>
                My task was designing a mobile application that generally had something to do with smart homes. Besides that we were free in choosing our specific app concept. 
            <p>
            <br>
                After contemplating a few ideas, I chose an app that would let pet owners control their smart bowl for automated feeding, analysing ones pets' eating behaviour and checking on how much food is still in the bowl at any given moment.
            <p>
            <br>
                I used the “Smart Napf” project primarily to get more familiar with designing and prototyping in Figma.
            </p>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <div slot="large-img-section">
        <Section>
            <img class="mx-auto h-full object-fill" src="/img/cubes/smartnapf/large.webp" />
            <p class="text-center py-2">
                Poster design for the rough “Smart Napf” design.
            </p>
        </Section>
    </div>
</ProjectLayout>